{"base_rate":0.42575558475689884,"brier":0.1313143232588699,"bss":0.4629002302455011,"bss_hi":0.5441205693097069,"bss_lo":0.3650069111292172,"chart":{"base":[430.0,118.0],"fp":[357.8,301.3],"lead":"62,277.4 272,248.1 482,200.7 692,122.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.46 — higher than 87% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +5pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 88% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 7%; promised 98% → rained 90%"},"rel":"62,436.3 150.7,339.5 506.7,142.7 681.7,75.3"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08567674113009198,"ess":343.20663382329514,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Hamburg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Hamburg rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>90%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nHAMBURG FUHLSBUETTEL, 9.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.46, ranked 29 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(11&ndash;71) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>276</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>96</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>90%</b></td><td class='num'>157</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Hamburg</b> <span class=\"muted\">Germany</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;43% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 43% of days.</p><p>The forecast did clearly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.46</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>11&ndash;71\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Hamburg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Hamburg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 77.728125,344.0833333333333 141.79388235294118,262.09411764705885 258.1661764705883,135.76470588235293 350.699746835443,54.860759493670855 406.22777070063694,18.0 406.22777070063694,31.910828025477713 350.699746835443,114.75949367088606 258.1661764705883,216.05882352941177 141.79388235294118,326.32941176470587 77.728125,374.4166666666667 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"227.02496714848883\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"227.02496714848883\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,356.94202898550725 77.728125,298.58333333333337 141.79388235294118,249.24705882352941 258.1661764705883,151.82352941176472 350.699746835443,73.29113924050637 406.22777070063694,52.77707006369428\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 276 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"356.94202898550725\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 96 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"77.728125\" cy=\"298.58333333333337\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 24%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"141.79388235294118\" cy=\"249.24705882352941\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 57%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"258.1661764705883\" cy=\"151.82352941176472\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"350.699746835443\" cy=\"73.29113924050637\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 157 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"406.22777070063694\" cy=\"52.77707006369428\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(43%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Hamburg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.59) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.31).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.307</td><td class='num'>12.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.429</td><td class='num'>9.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>0.494</td><td class='num'>9.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.591</td><td class='num'>6.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.55073,"lon":9.99302,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Hamburg","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":276,"obs":0.06884057971014493,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.05572916666666666,"n":96,"obs":0.22916666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":0.40000000000000174,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.23670588235294118,"n":85,"obs":0.36470588235294116,"sig":true},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.40000000000000174,"mean":0.5654411764705884,"n":68,"obs":0.6323529411764706,"sig":false},{"hi":0.93,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.8268354430379746,"n":79,"obs":0.8481012658227848,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.93,"mean":0.9836942675159236,"n":157,"obs":0.9044585987261147,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":9.3,"provisional":false,"rank":29,"rank_hi":71.02499999999998,"rank_lo":11.0,"reliability":0.009085692800168488,"resolution":0.1211009104765946,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"hamburg","station":"HAMBURG FUHLSBUETTEL","timezone":"Europe/Berlin"}